1
00:00:00,088 --> 00:00:04,208
One-thirty. Ten minutes before Marcus
called about the man on the ramp.

2
00:00:04,537 --> 00:00:06,967
They were cutting through the wall, Theo
said.

3
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:08,870
Loud as a chainsaw.

4
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:11,010
I could hear it all the way at the cinema.

5
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:13,293
He rubbed his sleeve over his nose.

6
00:00:13,769 --> 00:00:15,209
People started coming in.

7
00:00:15,229 --> 00:00:16,649
Through the service hall.

8
00:00:16,929 --> 00:00:19,943
They just kept coming. What did the woman
do?

9
00:00:20,347 --> 00:00:21,547
Told them to keep drilling.

10
00:00:22,881 --> 00:00:25,301
I sat on the bottom rung beside Theo.

11
00:00:25,541 --> 00:00:29,241
Through the door, I could hear somebody's
hand dragging over the wall.

12
00:00:29,381 --> 00:00:30,561
The woman on my radio?

13
00:00:30,761 --> 00:00:32,406
I asked. Same voice.

14
00:00:33,006 --> 00:00:34,846
I heard her in your store last night.

15
00:00:35,786 --> 00:00:39,358
You're sure? She was right below me when
they were drilling, Danny.

16
00:00:40,023 --> 00:00:42,153
I looked at the door. They saw them?

17
00:00:42,363 --> 00:00:44,692
Theo nodded. One of the men went to look.

18
00:00:44,932 --> 00:00:47,712
Came back running. The woman kept saying
another minute.

19
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:49,292
And then?

20
00:00:49,515 --> 00:00:52,295
They took the machine and went through the
staff door.

21
00:00:52,675 --> 00:00:54,675
I stayed where I was until it got quiet.

22
00:00:55,025 --> 00:00:56,245
The food court.

23
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:59,765
The broken glass. The service halls
filling up.

24
00:01:00,105 --> 00:01:03,705
I'd watched all those cameras and thought
the crowd was wandering through any

25
00:01:03,725 --> 00:01:04,585
door it found.

26
00:01:05,345 --> 00:01:06,685
I'd been watching where they went.

27
00:01:07,165 --> 00:01:08,725
Theo had heard what they were following.

28
00:01:09,005 --> 00:01:11,265
Was there a kid with them? Theo shook his
head.

29
00:01:11,285 --> 00:01:12,979
A little girl? No.

30
00:01:13,338 --> 00:01:15,078
I heard Vera's voice again.

31
00:01:15,298 --> 00:01:16,578
Soft through the speaker.

32
00:01:16,838 --> 00:01:18,958
The little girl had stopped asking for
food.

33
00:01:19,238 --> 00:01:22,058
I stood up too fast and hit my shoulder on
the ladder.

34
00:01:22,378 --> 00:01:24,698
Theo caught the container before it struck
the floor.

35
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:28,513
For a moment I wanted to go straight to
the department store.

36
00:01:28,933 --> 00:01:33,113
Stand outside her gate and make her tell
me why she'd kept that drill going.

37
00:01:33,813 --> 00:01:35,613
My keys were still wrapped in the sock.

38
00:01:36,033 --> 00:01:39,453
I closed my hand around them until the
teeth pressed through the fabric.

39
00:01:39,801 --> 00:01:41,387
Danny, Theo said.

40
00:01:41,787 --> 00:01:45,107
I looked at his leg. At the blood drying
on the edge of his trainer.

41
00:01:45,327 --> 00:01:48,407
He had followed me down here. Now he was
waiting for me to get him back.

42
00:01:48,647 --> 00:01:51,627
I picked up the water. On the return trip,
we moved around the broken

43
00:01:51,647 --> 00:01:53,547
section. It took nearly an hour.

44
00:01:53,827 --> 00:01:55,727
I could see my boot in the fountain below.

45
00:01:55,996 --> 00:01:57,456
I could see Marcus too.

46
00:02:21,976 --> 00:02:24,476
At the cinema, Theo stopped to pick up his
blanket.

47
00:02:24,716 --> 00:02:26,836
He tucked the photograph inside it.

48
00:02:26,976 --> 00:02:29,156
I pretended to be busy with the
containers.

49
00:02:29,616 --> 00:02:33,296
I got back to Summit Outdoors in one boot
and a filthy sock.

50
00:02:33,556 --> 00:02:36,396
Theo went down first and cleared a place
for the containers.

51
00:02:36,816 --> 00:02:38,596
Then he steadied the rack while I climbed.

52
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:41,960
I reached the floor and put my hand on the
padlock.

53
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,460
Closed. Exactly where I'd left it.

54
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,720
I let go and turned toward Theo.

55
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:50,660
He was sitting on the bucket, trying to
bend his trouser leg far enough to

56
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:53,960
see the cut. I'd checked that lock so many
times.

57
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:57,820
Theo had just brought me home without
going anywhere near it.

58
00:02:58,098 --> 00:02:59,598
I got the first-aid box.

59
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:02,378
At nine, I climbed to the roof alone.

60
00:03:02,998 --> 00:03:05,018
Three lights from Lily. Three back.

61
00:03:05,738 --> 00:03:09,138
I held the roof hatch open a little on the
way down, so I could see whether

62
00:03:09,158 --> 00:03:12,218
Theo was still there. He was asleep beside
the water.

63
00:03:13,578 --> 00:03:15,318
We'd got back the afternoon before.

64
00:03:15,658 --> 00:03:19,478
I'd used bottled water to clean the scrape
on his leg and found a bandage in

65
00:03:19,498 --> 00:03:22,878
the first-aid display. He'd let me do it
without looking at me once.

66
00:03:23,329 --> 00:03:25,309
I'd asked him to tell me if it got worse.

67
00:03:26,109 --> 00:03:26,949
He'd said he would,

68
00:03:27,729 --> 00:03:32,469
much too quickly. Later, I'd found him
putting the empty wrapper from his

69
00:03:32,489 --> 00:03:37,709
bandage inside another wrapper, folding
both down until they took up almost

70
00:03:37,729 --> 00:03:40,249
no room. He'd done the same with his food.

71
00:03:40,702 --> 00:03:44,242
I knew that habit. I'd seen it in the
places above the cinema.

72
00:03:44,602 --> 00:03:48,242
A whole life packed small enough that you
could move it before somebody told

73
00:03:48,262 --> 00:03:52,222
you to. That morning he was beside the
rack with his blanket rolled under one

74
00:03:52,242 --> 00:03:54,196
arm. Where are you going? Back.

75
00:03:54,616 --> 00:03:56,376
Your leg's hurting.

76
00:03:56,790 --> 00:04:00,031
It's fine. He shifted his weight onto the
other foot.

77
00:04:00,571 --> 00:04:04,851
I looked at the ceiling tile. His way out
was three shelves up, above the

78
00:04:04,871 --> 00:04:06,331
pipe he'd used while I slept.

79
00:04:07,011 --> 00:04:08,451
Pick a tent, I said.

80
00:04:08,731 --> 00:04:10,551
He watched me. Any of them.

81
00:04:10,931 --> 00:04:12,991
Except that one. I'm in that one.

82
00:04:13,214 --> 00:04:15,487
For how long? We'll work it out.

83
00:04:15,846 --> 00:04:20,418
What do you want? That question made me
put down the box I was holding.

84
00:04:20,878 --> 00:04:23,058
Help with the water. Keep things quiet.

85
00:04:23,398 --> 00:04:25,058
Tell me if you hear people up there.

86
00:04:25,238 --> 00:04:27,638
He waited. That's it, I said.

87
00:04:27,918 --> 00:04:29,998
I got him a clean sweatshirt from a shelf.

88
00:04:30,298 --> 00:04:34,198
He folded it so carefully before he put it
down that I had to find something

89
00:04:34,218 --> 00:04:37,223
else to look at. Vera called near dusk.

90
00:04:37,637 --> 00:04:39,617
Danny. Any room at the inn?

91
00:04:39,967 --> 00:04:42,087
I held the radio close to my ear.

92
00:04:42,415 --> 00:04:44,033
Still there? she asked.

93
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:47,533
I pressed the button. You said you were
trying on a coat.

94
00:04:47,821 --> 00:04:48,521
Yes.

95
00:04:49,864 --> 00:04:51,224
Before the mall closed.

96
00:04:51,586 --> 00:04:56,586
Eventually you're going to have to explain
this interest in my shopping.

97
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:59,486
Theo was watching me from the open tent.

98
00:04:59,806 --> 00:05:02,306
I let go of the button. Left her waiting
this time.

99
00:05:02,506 --> 00:05:04,966
At five to nine, I took the flashlight
from the shelf.

100
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:07,086
Theo pulled on the clean sweatshirt.

101
00:05:07,341 --> 00:05:08,870
Can I see? he asked.

102
00:05:10,231 --> 00:05:12,031
I let Theo come up with me.

103
00:05:12,171 --> 00:05:16,151
He stood a little behind the hatch,
keeping his weight off the bandaged leg.

104
00:05:16,391 --> 00:05:20,311
Across the highway, Parkview was barely
visible against the sky.

105
00:05:20,591 --> 00:05:23,931
I found the tenth floor. Counted to the
fourth window from the left.

106
00:05:24,285 --> 00:05:25,685
I always counted.

107
00:05:26,485 --> 00:05:27,965
Even when I already knew where to look.

108
00:05:28,205 --> 00:05:30,205
At nine, the flashlight came on.

109
00:05:30,505 --> 00:05:31,865
One. Two. Three.

110
00:05:32,145 --> 00:05:35,445
I answered with my own. My hands were
steadier than they'd been the night

111
00:05:35,465 --> 00:05:37,365
before. I had water downstairs.

112
00:05:37,805 --> 00:05:41,665
There was another person waiting beside
me, alive, who could hear something

113
00:05:41,685 --> 00:05:43,205
fall and help me pick it up.

114
00:05:43,516 --> 00:05:45,596
It came from the department store roof.

115
00:05:45,996 --> 00:05:47,576
One. Two. Three.

116
00:05:47,816 --> 00:05:48,916
Pointed across the highway.

117
00:05:48,936 --> 00:05:50,216
Toward her window.

118
00:05:51,496 --> 00:05:54,176
I lowered my flashlight. I wanted to blink
again.

119
00:05:54,556 --> 00:05:57,676
Correct it somehow. Tell Lily which light
was mine.

120
00:05:58,033 --> 00:06:01,773
But we had three flashes, and we had the
emergency signal.

121
00:06:02,013 --> 00:06:05,513
That was all. I'd never taught her what to
do when somebody else answered.

122
00:06:05,773 --> 00:06:09,633
My thumb rested on the switch while the
department store roof went dark.

123
00:06:09,873 --> 00:06:12,433
I kept it there until I was sure I
wouldn't press it.

124
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:14,433
Theo looked from that roof to me.

125
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:16,475
Who is that? he asked.

126
00:06:17,535 --> 00:06:19,895
I put the light in my pocket before I
answered.

127
00:06:21,095 --> 00:06:21,795
The woman.

128
00:06:23,195 --> 00:06:24,855
The radio stayed off.

129
00:06:26,315 --> 00:06:27,395
In front of us,

130
00:06:28,415 --> 00:06:29,655
Lily's window went dark.

131
00:06:31,155 --> 00:06:32,595
Our goodnight was over.

132
00:06:34,015 --> 00:06:35,415
Somebody else had joined it.

133
00:06:36,915 --> 00:06:39,415
I stood there until Theo touched my
sleeve.

134
00:06:39,926 --> 00:06:41,206
He was looking at the keys.

135
00:06:41,846 --> 00:06:44,486
The sock had come loose when I'd put the
flashlight away.

136
00:06:44,766 --> 00:06:47,406
The last red tag hung against my hand.

137
00:06:47,697 --> 00:06:49,851
What's B3? he asked.

138
00:06:50,151 --> 00:06:51,691
I looked down. Why?

139
00:06:52,061 --> 00:06:54,361
That woman. She kept saying it.

140
00:06:54,481 --> 00:06:56,721
Down to B3. Get to the door.

141
00:06:57,064 --> 00:06:59,624
I closed my fingers around the tag.

142
00:07:00,161 --> 00:07:03,041
They weren't trying to get into a shop, he
said.

143
00:07:03,618 --> 00:07:05,418
They were trying to get underneath it.

144
00:07:05,783 --> 00:07:08,923
I thought of Walt tapping the last key.

145
00:07:09,663 --> 00:07:12,363
Don't ask. Across the highway was my
daughter.

146
00:07:12,883 --> 00:07:15,623
Across the roof was a woman copying her
signal.

147
00:07:16,203 --> 00:07:19,083
And the thing that woman wanted was
hanging from my belt.

148
00:07:19,703 --> 00:07:21,663
What did she think was behind that door?
